    ! #223: "The assistant could claim a ticket change without a successful tool result or ask you to confirm a change you had already requested." - The live reproduction did not reproduce either reported behavior in five turns; the PR added a missing prompt policy, rather than fixing a behavior observed before this change.
    ! #223: "It now reports a change only after a tool call succeeds and proceeds with requested changes without asking again" - The PR added instructions to the system prompt and verified a live scenario, but says model behavior cannot be guaranteed by the scripted tests. This wording presents the policy as guaranteed behavior.
    ! #219: "so you can rely on those answers being assessed by meaning" - Semantic scoring is used when embeddings are available, but the PR says that path is nondeterministic and falls back to lexical scoring when embeddings are unavailable or fail. The assurance overstates what the change guarantees.

